      "title": "The first underwriter",
      "narration": "Before Rosa’s application reaches the home office, Theo has already underwritten it in her kitchen. Field underwriting means the producer’s screening of the applicant: observing her health and occupation, asking every question on the form, recording answers exactly as given and noting anything the insurer should know in the producer’s report. Good field underwriting saves the insurer from issuing policies it would have declined and saves applicants from policies that would be rescinded later for misstatements. It also protects the pool from adverse selection. The producer who skips this role invites claim disputes and license complaints.",
