      "title": "Errors and omissions",
      "narration": "Even careful producers make mistakes: a benefit amount misquoted, a replacement handled badly, an application mailed late so a client was uninsured when a claim arose. Errors and omissions insurance is professional liability coverage that pays defense costs and damages when a client sues over the producer’s negligent act or omission. It does not cover fraud, intentional misconduct or fines imposed by the regulator. Agencies carry it for the firm and its producers. The best E and O protection is process: documented recommendations, signed applications, delivery receipts and notes of what the client was told.",
