      "title": "Conditional receipt versus binding receipt",
      "text": "Most health insurers use conditional receipts: coverage is effective as of the application or medical exam date only if the applicant is found insurable as applied for. A binding receipt, which provides coverage from the application date regardless of insurability until the insurer acts, is uncommon in health insurance.",
